### Installation ###

You can install the `tree-sitter-cli` with `cargo`:

```sh
cargo install --locked tree-sitter-cli
```

or with `npm`:

```sh
npm install tree-sitter-cli
```

You can also download a pre-built binary
for your platform from [the releases page].

### Dependencies ### 

The `tree-sitter` binary itself has no dependencies, 
 but specific commands have dependencies that must be present at runtime:

* To generate a parser from a grammar, you must have [`node`](https://nodejs.org) on your PATH.
* To run and test parsers, you must have a C and C++ compiler on your system.
 
